{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2180-02-15 17:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. Can you tell me what brought you in today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2180-02-15 17:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’ve been having a lot more diarrhea—watery, not bloody—and this constant abdominal pain, especially on the left side. It feels like my Crohn’s is flaring again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2180-02-15 17:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And how long has this been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2180-02-15 17:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "About a week. I tried increasing my prednisone from 10 mg to 35 mg, thinking it was a flare, but it didn’t help at all."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2180-02-15 17:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Any fevers, chills, or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2180-02-15 17:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No fevers or vomiting. But I do feel nauseous when I sit up. Haven’t thrown up though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2180-02-15 17:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. We’ve already given you IV ciprofloxacin in the ER and started IV steroids. We’re going to keep you on IV fluids and hold off on food for now to let your gut rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2180-02-15 17:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No food? How long will that be?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2180-02-15 17:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just for a day or two, depending on how you respond. We want to reduce inflammation and make sure there’s no infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2180-02-15 17:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I’ve been through this before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2180-02-15 17:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also did a CT scan of your abdomen and pelvis. Let me go over the results with you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2180-02-15 17:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, please. I’ve been worried about a blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2180-02-15 17:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The scan shows a 5 cm narrowed segment of bowel just above your ileorectal anastomosis, with some inflammation in the surrounding tissue. This looks like long-standing Crohn’s changes. No blockage or perforation, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2180-02-15 17:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not a full obstruction?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2180-02-15 17:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, not a complete blockage. But there may be a partial slowdown, which could explain your symptoms. We also noticed your stomach is quite distended, which might mean delayed emptying."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2180-02-15 17:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That could explain the nausea when I sit up. What about infection? Could this be something I ate?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2180-02-15 17:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We tested your stool. No sign of Salmonella, Shigella, C. diff, or parasites. So it doesn’t look like an infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2180-02-15 17:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to know. So it’s probably just my Crohn’s acting up again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2180-02-15 17:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most likely. Your GI team thinks the pain is multifactorial—chronic inflammation, adhesions from past surgeries, and possibly some partial slowing in the bowel."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2180-02-15 17:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. I’ve had so many surgeries. I just want to get back to feeling stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2180-02-16 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2180-02-16 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Morning, Doctor. The pain is a bit better, but I’m still nauseous when I move."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2180-02-16 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs this morning show your white count is stable, and kidney function is normal. We’re going to keep you NPO a little longer but may try a clear liquid diet tomorrow if you keep improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2180-02-16 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And the steroids—are we still doing IV?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2180-02-16 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, another dose today. Once you start tolerating food, we’ll switch you back to oral prednisone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2180-02-16 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was on 10 mg before, but I bumped it up to 35 mg. Should I go back to 10?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2180-02-16 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll discharge you on 30 mg daily. Your GI doctor will help you taper it down safely at your follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2180-02-16 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds better than what I was doing on my own."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2180-02-16 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to start you on clear liquids this afternoon. If you tolerate that, we can advance your diet tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2180-02-16 14:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. I’m ready to try something. Any restrictions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2180-02-16 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just start slow—water, broth, apple juice. Let the nurse know if you feel nauseous or bloated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2180-02-17 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you tolerated the liquids well. We’re going to switch you to a soft diet this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2180-02-17 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. When can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2180-02-17 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you do well with breakfast, we’re planning to discharge you this afternoon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2180-02-17 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Perfect. What meds will I be going home with?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2180-02-17 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take prednisone 30 mg daily, finish the ciprofloxacin for five days, omeprazole, loperamide as needed, and Percocet for pain if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2180-02-17 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my B12 shots?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2180-02-17 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue those monthly. Also, don’t forget your flu vaccine—we’ll give you that before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2180-02-17 07:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I hadn’t thought about that. Thanks for reminding me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2180-02-17 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. Make sure to follow up with GI, your surgeon, and your primary doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2180-02-17 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I know I’m at risk for flare-ups, so I’ll keep an eye on things."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2180-02-17 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Call us if the pain worsens, or if you develop fever or vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2180-02-17 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thanks for taking such good care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2180-02-17 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take it easy, and we’ll see you in clinic soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2180-02-15 17:18:00",
    "admission_end": "2180-02-17 15:30:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A male patient with a history of Crohn’s disease and multiple prior abdominal surgeries was admitted for increased watery diarrhea and abdominal pain, which he initially attributed to a flare and self-managed by increasing his prednisone dose. Imaging revealed a 5 cm segment of narrowed bowel with mesenteric fat stranding near the ileorectal anastomosis, consistent with chronic Crohn’s changes and a possible mild acute component, but no obstruction or perforation. Stool studies were negative for infectious causes. He was managed with bowel rest, IV fluids, IV steroids, and IV ciprofloxacin. His symptoms improved, and he successfully advanced to a soft diet. He was discharged home on oral prednisone 30 mg daily, a five-day course of ciprofloxacin, and pain medication, with follow-up arranged with gastroenterology, surgery, and primary care. A flu vaccine was administered prior to discharge.",
    "problems": [
      "Regional enteritis of small intestine with large intestine",
      "Intestinal bypass or anastomosis status",
      "Tobacco use disorder",
      "Need for prophylactic vaccination and inoculation against influenza"
    ]
  }
}
